# shir_nodes/foreach_line.node — STREAMING line iteration over a file.
#
# The dynamic-source primitive: reduces `cmd file` / `grep P F | cmd`
# pipelines to a lazy per-line loop — O(1) memory (O(limit) for early-exit
# heads), never slurps the file where bash itself streams. Body statements
# use the existing VALUE primitives (FieldExtract/Contains/RegSub/…) per
# line. limit=None reads to EOF; Some(expr) stops after that many lines
# (`head -n K F`) — backends close the reader early.
#
# Backends: Perl while(<$fh>)+last, JS sh2.eachLine(path,cb,limit),
# C getline, Go bufio.Scanner, Zig reader loop.

node ForEachLine
tag "ForEachLine"
field source: expr
field var: string
field body: stmts
field limit: optional_expr
# RESOLVED — the contract is the STREAM POSITION AND COST model, defined in the theory as
# ordinary functions over the same `lines_of` model the value side uses:
#   line_count s   = length (lines_of s)                      -- how many lines are emitted
#   lines_len s    = sum of the emitted line lengths           -- payload bytes
#   line_pos ls k  = sum over the first k lines of (len + 1)   -- bytes consumed before line k
#   line_start s k = line_pos (lines_of s) k
# All obligations are proved and bundled in TextOps#foreach_line_sound:
#  * VALUE: join_lf (lines_of s) = s (TextOps#lines_of_join_sound, from
#    TextOps#split_lf_rebuild and TextOps#join_lf_snoc).
#  * COST AND COVERAGE, not a set equality: lines_len s + line_count s = length s + 1
#    (TextOps#lines_of_cost, via TextOps#join_lf_cost and TextOps#sum_list_suc_len) — the
#    emitted lines and the newlines between them account for the whole input exactly once.
#  * POSITION: for every k < line_count s, drop (line_start s k) s = join_lf (drop k (lines_of s))
#    (TextOps#lines_of_position, via TextOps#line_pos_join_take, TextOps#join_lf_take_drop,
#    TextOps#join_lf_append and TextOps#drop_suc_length_append) — dropping the bytes already
#    consumed lands exactly on line k, so each emitted line's position is its offset, and the
#    reader resumes at the start of the next line.
#  * NO DUPLICATE POSITIONS: line_start s k < line_start s (Suc k) for every emitted k
#    (TextOps#line_start_strict, via TextOps#line_start_Suc), with TextOps#take_nonempty
#    supplying the arithmetic — so no line is emitted twice and the segments tile the source.
# LIMIT: `limit: Some k` emits take k (lines_of s); TextOps#lines_of_append_nl,
# TextOps#join_lf_of_append_nl and TextOps#lines_of_nil cover the trailing-newline and
# empty-string edge cases.
# NON-VACUITY: TextOps#foreach_line_witness checks the positions and the coverage identity on
# [97, nl, nl, 98, nl] — a blank line in the middle plus a trailing newline, so the last
# emitted line is empty. TextOps#dup_lines_same_set_wrong_count is a fold with the SAME
# emitted set and a wrong count, and TextOps#shifted_position_rejected is a position rule off
# by one; both are rejected by the contract, while TextOps#position_accepted satisfies the
# position law on the same input.
# NOT PROMISED (outside this model): IO errors and partial reads, reader close timing, and
# memory/laziness — the model is over a complete byte string, so "never slurps" (O(1) memory,
# O(limit) for early-exit heads) is an implementation property of the backends above, not a
# theorem here; entry metadata and encoding are likewise out of scope.
spec: TextOps#foreach_line_sound
